.TH INITTAB 5 "August 4, 2026" "ReBSD" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
inittab \- System V process initialization table
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I /etc/inittab
file describes the processes started and supervised by
.BR init (8).
Each entry has four colon-separated fields:
.PP
.RS
.I id:runlevels:action:process
.RE
.PP
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.  A backslash immediately before a newline continues an entry.
A complete logical entry may contain at most 512 bytes.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.I id
A unique identifier containing one through four characters.
.TP
.I runlevels
Zero or more of
.BR 0 \- 6 ,
.BR S ,
.BR s ,
.BR a ,
.BR b ,
and
.BR c .
The
.BR a ,
.BR b ,
and
.B c
levels are on-demand levels.
.TP
.I action
One of the actions described below.
.TP
.I process
A command executed as
.BR "sh -c 'exec process'" .
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B sysinit
Wait for the process during early system initialization, before init opens
the console.  Runlevels are ignored.  All
.B sysinit
entries finish before any boot action begins.
.TP
.B boot
Start the process without waiting the first time init enters a matching
non-single-user runlevel after boot.
.TP
.B bootwait
Start the process and wait for it the first time init enters a matching
non-single-user runlevel after boot.
.TP
.B initdefault
Select the initial runlevel.  If several real runlevels are specified, the
highest numbered level is selected.  An empty runlevel field means
.B 0123456
and therefore selects level 6.  The process field is empty.
.TP
.B respawn
Start the process whenever the selected runlevel is active and restart it
after it exits.
.TP
.B ondemand
Like
.BR respawn ,
but selected only by a request for runlevel
.BR a ,
.BR b ,
or
.BR c .
.TP
.B once
Start the process once when entering a selected runlevel without waiting.
.TP
.B wait
Start the process when entering a selected runlevel and wait for it.
.TP
.B powerfail
Start the process after
.B SIGPWR
without waiting.
.TP
.B powerwait
Start the process after
.B SIGPWR
and wait for it.
.TP
.B off
Do not start the entry and stop its existing process when the table is
reloaded.  The process field may be empty.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
is::sysinit:/etc/rc.sysinit
id:2:initdefault:
r2:2:wait:/etc/rc 2
su:S:respawn:/bin/sh
co:2345:respawn:/libexec/getty std.default console
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR init (8),
.BR getty (8)
